WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.777
The first project step is inspection.

00:00:02.777 --> 00:00:09.167
In a Spark notebook, the print schema command helps you inspect column names and data types.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:12.417
A show command lets you look at sample rows.

00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:20.462
A count action can tell you how many records exist, but remember that counting a distributed dataset triggers

00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:23.032
computation. Use these tools intentionally.

00:00:23.032 --> 00:00:29.262
Before you clean or aggregate anything, answer the same questions you have used throughout the course.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.172
What columns do I have?

00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:32.997
What types do they use?

00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:36.963
Are values missing? And what does one raw row represent?
